      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surface segregation of lower-melting constituents primarily governs premelting and melting in Fe–Ni–Cr–Co–Cu nanoparticles.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11775865::rubric_card::000::48472d49c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Segregation is thermodynamically driven by surface-energy minimization.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Copper and possibly cobalt have the lower melting points and surface energies needed to drive their outward migration in this alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surface enrichment in copper or cobalt reduces local cohesive energy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The compositionally enriched, locally weakened surface premelts below the temperature for complete nanoparticle melting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surface melting subsequently propagates inward and melts the entire particle.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heating will produce a detectable liquid-like and compositionally distinct surface layer before complete melting.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Fe–Ni–Cr–Co–Cu nanoparticles will exhibit two-stage melting, with the surface melting before the core.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Uniformly mixed single-metal or simpler-alloy baseline nanoparticles do not significantly segregate and therefore melt in a single uniform transition.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
